Today is Wednesday, it is now afternoon.
Rohan and I come outside from the office building.
Our office is very air-conditioned.
We walk outside for a short rest.
Near the office, there is a small tea shop.
We go near the tea vendor.
I say to him, "Brother, please give two cutting chais."
He quickly gives us hot cutting chai.
Rohan asks me, "Maya, how is your work going?"
I say, "The project work is good."
"Today I have written new code."
Rohan smiles, and drinks his tea.
We converse about life in Mumbai city.
Rohan says, "The life of Mumbai city is very fast."
I say, "True."
"But I like it here."
"I have learned many new things here," I say.
"And I have found good friends here."
This hot cutting chai removes our tiredness.
This short rest gives me new energy.
After ten minutes, we go back to the office.
